3. Brief facts of the case are as under;
That on 04.07.2017 at about 12.00 noon, the claimant was riding motor cycle bearing registration No.KA-07-Y-9432, when he reached near Ajjappanahalli gate on Bengaluru- Chennai NH-75 road,
Kolar taluk and district.

14. Accordingly, I pass the following:
 ORDER  i) The appeal is allowed-in-part;
 ii) The judgment and award dated 03.03.2020 passed by XIX Additional Judge and Motor Accident Claims Tribunal, Bengaluru in MVC.No.6206/2017 is modified;
iii) The claimant would be entitled to a sum of Rs.7,05,000/- as against Rs.4,54,100/-;
iv) The enhanced compensation amount shall be paid by the respondent-Insurance Company with interest @ 6% per annum within a period of four weeks from the date of receipt of a copy of this order;
v) All other terms and conditions stipulated by the tribunal shall stand intact.

